        "id": "def-qc-tqc-fixed-charge-encoding",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Fixed-charge encoding and code projector",
        "statement_or_definition": "Let $V=V(x^n\\to c)\\ne0$ be the finite-dimensional fixed-total-charge fusion\nspace for $n$ identical charges $x$, equipped with the unitary fusion-tree\ninner product from [[def-qc-tqc-fusion-tree-basis]]. Let\n$\\mathcal C=\\mathbb C^k$ with its ordered orthonormal computational basis,\nwhere $k\\ge1$. A **fixed-charge encoding** is an isometry\n$J:\\mathcal C\\to V$, so $J^*J=I_{\\mathcal C}$. Its code subspace is\n$J\\mathcal C$, and its code projector is\n$$P:=JJ^*:V\\to V.$$\nAn encoding records a chosen subspace of a fusion space; it does not identify\nthat subspace with an object of the fusion category.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qc-tqc-fusion-tree-basis",
          "def-fusion-and-multifusion-category",
          "def-qc-tqc-unitary-fusion-category",
          "def-linear-isometry-and-orthogonal-or-unitary-operator",
          "def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 4,
        "proof_obligations": [
          "1.1 By [F2], $P^*=(JJ^*)^*=(J^*)^*J^*=JJ^*=P$. Also\n$P^2=JJ^*JJ^*=J(J^*J)J^*=JI_{\\mathcal C}J^*=P$ by [F1]. Hence $P$ is an\northogonal projection. [given, F1, F2, algebra]",
          "1.2 For every $u\\in\\mathcal C$, $P(Ju)=JJ^*Ju=Ju$ by [F1], so\n$J\\mathcal C\\subseteq\\operatorname{ran}P$. Conversely $Pv=J(J^*v)$ lies\nin $J\\mathcal C$ for every $v\\in V$, so\n$\\operatorname{ran}P\\subseteq J\\mathcal C$. Therefore\n$\\operatorname{ran}P=J\\mathcal C$. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎"
