      {
        "id": "thm-qc-tqc-block-approximation-error",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Block-target approximation bounds logical error and leakage",
        "statement_or_definition": "Let $V=P V\\oplus(I-P)V$ be an orthogonal decomposition of a finite-dimensional\nHilbert space, let $U$ and $W$ be unitary operators on the two summands, and\nlet $T:=U\\oplus W$. If an ambient unitary $G$ satisfies\n$\\|G-T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\le\\delta$, then the logical block error of $G$ relative\nto $U$ and its leakage amplitude both are at most $\\delta$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qc-tqc-logical-error-and-leakage",
          "def-operator-norm-on-a-finite-dimensional-inner-product-space"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "proof_obligations": [
          "1.1 If $V=0$, both error maps have norm zero by [F2], so both bounds hold. Otherwise, since $T$ preserves both summands, $PTP=UP$ on $V$ and $(I-P)TP=0$. Thus $PGP-UP=P(G-T)P$. For any $y\\in V$, the orthogonal decomposition $y=Py+(I-P)y$ gives $\\|Py\\|\\le\\|y\\|$ and $\\|(I-P)y\\|\\le\\|y\\|$ by the Pythagorean identity. Hence for every unit vector $x$, $\\|P(G-T)Px\\|\\le\\|(G-T)Px\\|\\le\\|G-T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\|Px\\|\\le\\delta$. Taking the maximum in [F2] proves the logical block error bound. [given, F1, F2, algebra]",
          "2.1 In the remaining case $V\\ne0$, $(I-P)GP=(I-P)(G-T)P$ because $(I-P)TP=0$. By the contractions in step 1.1, for every unit $x$, $\\|(I-P)(G-T)Px\\|\\le\\|(G-T)Px\\|\\le\\|G-T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\|Px\\|\\le\\delta$. Taking the maximum gives the leakage bound. [given, F1, F2, step 1.1, algebra] ∎\n"
        ],
