          "1.2 Since $(\\gamma_j\\gamma_{j+1})^2=-I$, expansion of the exponential gives\n$U_j=2^{-1/2}(I-\\gamma_j\\gamma_{j+1})$. Its restrictions to\n$\\operatorname{ran}Q_1(j)$ and $\\operatorname{ran}Q_\\psi(j)$ are respectively\n$e^{-i\\pi/4}I$ and $e^{i\\pi/4}I$. Using the phase ratio in [F1] as imposed\nfor every generator by the interface, the channel exchange equals\n$$R_1Q_1(j)+R_\\psi Q_\\psi(j)=R_1e^{i\\pi/4}U_j.$$\nThus it differs from $U_j$ by one common scalar. [given, F1, algebra] ∎"
